\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Volatile sessions are detected almost perfectly; the \emph  {mean-reverting} regime is the systematic weak point. \textbf  {Important caveat for (b):} the per-trial logs we record contain the per-regime diagonal accuracy but not the predicted-vs-true regime pair on incorrect sessions. The off-diagonals shown here are therefore \emph  {reconstructed} by equally splitting $1-\text  {diagonal}$ across the two other columns, which is the maximum-entropy assumption given the available data. The matrix is indicative of the per-regime difficulty ranking only; the specific off-diagonal split is not measured. This is listed as a logging gap in \S  \ref {sec:discussion}.}}{10}{figure.caption.15}\protected@file@percent }
